<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/06/aqara-g5-pro-airpods-slate-7-composite-wide-1791313711028-932122353d.png" alt=""><p class="image-caption"></p></div>
<p id="p2">Amazon’s Big Deal Days for Prime members has begun, and we’ve collected some of our favorite deals offered. As usual, we’ve kept our picks simple, including only those that we’ve reviewed, use ourselves, or that are from brands we trust.</p>
<p id="p3">It’s worth noting that this sales event is focused on Prime members, so many of the deals require a Prime subscription. However, not all do.</p>
<h2 id="smart-home">Smart Home</h2>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/06/philips-hue-festavia-16x9-1791312290137-558d30411c.png" alt="Philips Hue Festavia lights on my balcony."><p class="image-caption">Philips Hue Festavia lights on my balcony.</p></div>
<p id="p5">I’m a big fan of <a href="https://amzn.to/4B77ozw" rel="noopener noreferrer">Philips Hue Festavia</a> string lights, which <a href="https://www.macstories.net/reviews/adding-colorful-animated-flare-to-the-holiday-season-with-hues-festavia-lights/" rel="noopener noreferrer">I reviewed on MacStories in 2023</a>. I hung a strand on our balcony, which has provided great outdoor atmosphere year-round.</p>
<p id="p6">The lights are great for the holidays, too. The Hue app lets you pick all sorts of festive presets that animate and color the lights to mimic candles, stars, and more. Festavia lights are also compatible with Apple’s Home app, giving you multiple ways to control and automate them, which I love. Both the <a href="https://amzn.to/4jd96ZH" rel="noopener noreferrer">65-foot</a> and <a href="https://amzn.to/4hFMIWd" rel="noopener noreferrer">130-foot</a> models are on sale.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/06/aqara-g5-pro-poe-16x9-1791312297776-bfcddd0237.png" alt="Aqara G5 Pro camera."><p class="image-caption">Aqara G5 Pro camera.</p></div>
<p id="p8">The <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DPX6H1FY?ref=t_ac_spc_accepted_tile&amp;linkCode=tr1&amp;tag=macstories00-20&amp;linkId=B0DPX6H1FY_1787743741417" rel="noopener noreferrer">Aqara G5 Pro camera is on sale</a>, too. It’s been over 18 months since <a href="https://www.macstories.net/reviews/rugged-reliable-and-homekit-ready-a-review-of-aqaras-g5-pro-outdoor-camera-hub/" rel="noopener noreferrer">I wrote about this sturdy and reliable outdoor HomeKit security camera</a>, and it’s still one of our most popular hardware reviews on the site. There’s a reason for that, too. The G5 Pro serves as a hub for your other Aqara devices, and stays connected reliably with clear nighttime footage, support for HomeKit Secure Video, and an onboard spotlight. Mine has been installed outside my home ever since I reviewed it, and it’s never missed a beat. I use <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DPX6H1FY?ref=t_ac_spc_accepted_tile&amp;linkCode=tr1&amp;tag=macstories00-20&amp;linkId=B0DPX6H1FY_1787743741417" rel="noopener noreferrer">the Wi-Fi model</a>, but <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DPX6H1FY?ref=t_ac_spc_accepted_tile&amp;linkCode=tr1&amp;tag=macstories00-20&amp;linkId=B0DPX6H1FY_1787743741417" rel="noopener noreferrer">the PoE version</a> is on sale too.</p>
<h2 id="travel-accessories-and-headphones">Travel Accessories and Headphones</h2>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/06/anker-prime-power-bank-16x9-1791312299046-11dd264687.png" alt="Anker's 20,100mAh Prime power bank"><p class="image-caption">Anker’s 20,100mAh Prime power bank</p></div>
<p id="p10">I’m a big fan of batteries and one of the best is <a href="https://amzn.to/4z9tkYI" rel="noopener noreferrer">Anker’s 20,100mAh Prime power bank</a>, which <a href="https://www.macstories.net/setups/#batteries-and-chargers" rel="noopener noreferrer">Federico added to his setup</a> just <a href="https://www.macstories.net/news/macstories-setups-update-batteries-chargers-e-ink-note-taking-and-videogames/" rel="noopener noreferrer">before WWDC this year</a>. I have a similar model, which is great for use with a laptop and other devices because it can deliver 220W of power with one USB-C port delivering 140W of charging.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/06/ugreen-qi2-power-bank-16x9-1791312397789-167d74d861.png" alt="UGREEN's 20,000mAh Qi 2 battery."><p class="image-caption">UGREEN’s 20,000mAh Qi 2 battery.</p></div>
<p id="p12">Another interesting battery option is <a href="https://amzn.to/4hLcfgK" rel="noopener noreferrer">UGREEN’s 20,000mAh Qi 2 battery</a> that delivers 25W of wireless power. I haven’t used this exact battery before, but I have a similar UGREEN model with a smaller capacity that I like a lot. This model also has a built-in USB-C cable and digital screen that shows how much charge is left.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/06/ugreen-nexode-pro-100w-charger-16x9-1791312807234-1b5d1bb7b0.png" alt="UGREEN's 100W Nexode Pro GaN charger"><p class="image-caption">UGREEN’s 100W Nexode Pro GaN charger</p></div><p><br>
A good travel wall charger is a must, too. When I’m on the road with my MacBook Pro, I always bring <a href="https://amzn.to/4i54VOq" rel="noopener noreferrer">UGREEN’s 100W Nexode Pro GaN charger</a>. It has two USB-C ports and one USB-A port, and its prongs fold flat so it’s easy to pack. Combined with its small size, it’s a great choice for any trip.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/06/gl-inet-slate-7-16x9-1791312300988-ee7e5b95f3.png" alt="Slate 7."><p class="image-caption">Slate 7.</p></div>
<p id="p15">A portable Wi-Fi router is great for traveling with your family when you want to stream a movie at night or when you’re working away from home at a coffee shop. My favorite is <a href="https://amzn.to/479sGi7" rel="noopener noreferrer">the Slate 7 by GL.iNet</a>, which <a href="https://www.macstories.net/news/macstories-setups-update-fresh-approaches-wi-fi-upgrades-and-handhelds/" rel="noopener noreferrer">I covered on MacStories last summer</a>. It works well to extend an existing network or to connect to your iPhone to create an ad hoc wireless network.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/06/satechi-usb-c-ethernet-adapter-16x9-1791312805854-74d16848b0.png" alt="Satechi USB-C 2.5Gbps Ethernet adapter."><p class="image-caption">Satechi USB-C 2.5Gbps Ethernet adapter.</p></div>
<p id="p17">Finally, I wanted to mention the <a href="https://amzn.to/4y5pC1w" rel="noopener noreferrer">Satechi USB-C 2.5Gbps Ethernet adapter</a>, which I carry whenever I stay in a hotel room because even slow Ethernet is better than most hotel Wi-Fi. I’ve had this adapter for a couple of years and it’s been a lifesaver on the road more than once, including at WWDC this year where I found myself uploading 4K video to YouTube from the Mountain View public library.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/06/airpods-pro-3-16x9-1791312302120-eacd82e629.png" alt="AirPods Pro 3."><p class="image-caption">AirPods Pro 3.</p></div>
<p id="p19">My favorite wireless earbuds and over-the-ear headphones are on sale too. <a href="https://amzn.to/47DqEa9" rel="noopener noreferrer">AirPods Pro 3</a> are my go-to everyday headphones for walking around the neighborhood or working remotely. The active noise cancelation is top tier, and I love both transparency mode for hearing what’s happening around me and the fit.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/06/beats-studio-pro-light-blue-16x9-1791312303431-d1164a273c.png" alt="Beats Studio Pro in Light Blue."><p class="image-caption">Beats Studio Pro in Light Blue.</p></div>
<p id="p21">I’m also a fan of <a href="https://amzn.to/474K7jW" rel="noopener noreferrer">the Beats Studio Pro headphones</a> for their versatility. They work wirelessly, with a 3.5mm headphone cable, or a USB-C cable, with both cables packed in the box. The sound and noise cancelation are excellent, too. Today’s sales price is one of the lowest I’ve seen, so it’s a great time to pick up a pair.</p>
